<h2>Questions from Atlanta property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do historic preservation rules affect my Atlanta claim?</summary><div class="a"><p>They can. Properties in locally designated districts may require approved materials or methods. When those requirements increase the cost of repair, policy ordinance-or-law provisions may come into play.</p></div></details><details><summary>My condo building’s HOA is also filing. Do I file separately?</summary><div class="a"><p>Often yes. The association’s master policy covers parts of the building it insures; your HO-6 covers your unit improvements and contents. We help figure out which policy covers what.</p></div></details></div>
